Thanks a lot, man.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:49.095
-Wow. [ Chuckles ]
Are you crying? Are you crying?

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:52.332
-No, I would never cry. It's
just someone's cutting onions.

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.332
-Oh, you're talking about a
flagel?

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:56.169
That's totally different.
-Oh.

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:58.371
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:02.508
Right, you ever have a flagel?
-I've had plenty of bialies.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.844
[ Laughter ]
-Quest, flagel?

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:08.647
-Nah, no.

00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:11.651
-Can we google a flagel,
is that real?

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:12.985
It's different than a bialy.
-Totally different.

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:16.955
-What is a bialy? Bialy --
Yeah, onions.

00:04:16.955 --> 00:04:20.226
-No, not always. Bialy does not
always have onions.

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:21.694
-Whoa wait, whoa.
-Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.930
-Hey, you don't have to upset.
-My God, Bobby Flay called.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.131
[ Laughter ]
-Flagel, bialy.

00:04:26.131 --> 00:04:27.767
-Okay, okay.
-That's the last time we go.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.368
-Alright.
-So he got upset or not.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:31.103
-My wife and kids are in the
audience.

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:33.005
-Yeah.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:36.709
-Guys, is a flagel
the same thing as a bialy?

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.044
